export const body = "<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>\n\n<ul><li>Introduction</li><li>The Original Goal</li><li>The First Result</li><li>The Second Result</li><li>The Preparation</li><li>The Scope</li><li>The Writing</li><li>The Illustration</li><li>The updating process</li><li>Explain first</li><li>One size does not fit all</li><li>In case you want to read</li><li>Closing</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Introduction</h3>\n\n<p>Two years ago, a team began working on the project—a VR first-person shooter set in World War II. During the development, artists often asked TAs for support on <em>minor</em> hiccups. To reduce stress on TAs and improve artists’ performance, the team decided to write a solution book serving as an optimization guide for newcomers.</p>\n\n<p>In this article, we will share with you their approach to this practice, as well as their process.<a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/38152f968e7fbbac4a62.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/38152f968e7fbbac4a62.webp\" width=\"770\" height=\"1000\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<h3>The Original Goal</h3>\n\n<p>When the artist (one of the authors) was still an artist, he usually needed help from a TA. Both of them went through a same script over and over, and they were tired of that. So, the artist decided to write this book to educate himself on those technical issues and to share it with other artists later.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d55be89df46aab0bbbed.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d55be89df46aab0bbbed.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"605\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 2\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/d845ee7fe8c812108a8f.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/d845ee7fe8c812108a8f.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"589\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 3\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p>There were two notable results from having the book.</p>\n\n<h3>The First Result</h3>\n\n<p>That FAQ document helped artists identify and solve many issues themselves. Because of that, the TA team had more time to work on more serious tasks, and the artists could focus more on the artistic quality rather than technical problems.</p>\n\n<p>After a while, TAs even stopped doing quality-check before submitting to clients.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/0779772baa9e12de2fdb.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/0779772baa9e12de2fdb.webp\" width=\"600\" height=\"338\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 4\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><em>TAs can’t quality-check if your assets are high-quality.</em><em><br></em></p>\n\n<p><em><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/00889b9ccc4a4d2d1c0a.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/00889b9ccc4a4d2d1c0a.webp\" width=\"1032\" height=\"582\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 5\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></em></p>\n\n<p>Nothing could interrupt their creative process anymore.</p>\n\n<h3>The Second Result</h3>\n\n<p>Since the book introduced artists to the technical side of development, it also familiarized them with the pipeline and terminology used by TAs. This newfound knowledge allowed them to communicate more precisely when they were in trouble. It was a relief to the whole team because every doctor loves a well-informed patient.</p>\n\n<p><strong><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/a48024c2307e5044a3e4.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/a48024c2307e5044a3e4.webp\" width=\"846\" height=\"1000\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 6\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></strong></p>\n\n<h3>The Preparation</h3>\n\n<p>The team started writing this document with their most recent problem back then: how it happened, and how it was resolved. Then, they outline the content with specific goals and scope.</p>\n\n<p>Analyze your latest problem to extract experience.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/3f3ee428cb74c9613f97.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/3f3ee428cb74c9613f97.webp\" width=\"872\" height=\"486\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 7\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p>Know what you build.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c2bb7ff7d079c240e009.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c2bb7ff7d079c240e009.webp\" width=\"968\" height=\"690\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 8\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<h3>The Scope</h3>\n\n<p>Knowing that the target readers of this book were junior artists, the team only added the fundamentals to avoid scope creep*. Advanced knowledge, therefore, was only shared and discussed within the TA circle.</p>\n\n<p><em>*Scope creep refers to the unintended and negative expansion of content due to poor management. Sometimes less is more.</em></p>\n\n<p><em><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/8e43f951a125d13902c2.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/8e43f951a125d13902c2.webp\" width=\"1022\" height=\"1000\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 9\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></em></p>\n\n<h3>The Writing</h3>\n\n<p>The actual writing process can be quite challenging because artists may not understand the language of TAs. Luckily, it was written by a former artist, so it had the artist perspective.</p>\n\n<p>The takeaway is choosing someone that can speak to your target audience to write documents for them.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/5aeeca6991ea8e7b414a.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/5aeeca6991ea8e7b414a.webp\" width=\"769\" height=\"1000\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 10\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<h3>The Illustration</h3>\n\n<p>Another challenge was finding the right pictures to get their points across. Although there are plenty of sources to draw from on the Internet, certain concepts just don’t have suitable illustrations. In this case, these are 4 recommended tips to work around it:</p>\n\n<ul><li>Use an analogy</li><li>Humanize the subject</li><li>Quote something well-known and relatable</li><li>Add an emoji</li></ul>\n\n<div class=\"source-panel\"><p><strong>EXAMPLE</strong></p><p><strong>Using analogies</strong></p>\n<p>For example, you can use the brain and library to explain the differences between RAM and HDD.</p>\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/72878b406192c4edaadb.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/72878b406192c4edaadb.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"769\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 11\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span><strong>Using quotes</strong></p>\n<p>Some famous sayings from two influential figures in the game industry regarding patience.</p>\n<p><strong><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/66f3889e294c3d130b32.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/66f3889e294c3d130b32.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"390\" style=\"--source-width:561px\" alt=\"Illustration 12\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></strong><strong><br></strong></p></div>\n\n<h3>The updating process</h3>\n\n<p>Similar to other TA groups, the team dedicated one person to this task; he tried to add new relevant knowledge to the book as soon as possible (instead of sticking to a schedule) and inform the artists via a group email.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/4361924c885f73232446.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/4361924c885f73232446.webp\" width=\"708\" height=\"1000\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 13\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<h3>Explain first</h3>\n\n<p>Another tip to bridge the gap between TAs and artists is <em>explain first</em>. An artist should understand the cause of a problem before he sees its solution.</p>\n\n<p>This way, artists could get a firm grasp on optimization, which in turn helps them avoid repeating the same mistake.</p>\n\n<p><strong><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/e3c2786f6c53add30a8c.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/e3c2786f6c53add30a8c.webp\" width=\"930\" height=\"1000\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 14\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></strong></p>\n\n<h3>One size does not fit all</h3>\n\n<p>As always, this is not an all-encompassing approach. It only suits end-to-end projects in which artists follow from start to finish.</p>\n\n<p>For other projects, in which people change teams frequently, the specific content of the document will not yield them enough long-term benefit.</p>\n\n<p><strong><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/af6e4fb88a7c3cea0491.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/af6e4fb88a7c3cea0491.webp\" width=\"821\" height=\"1000\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 15\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></strong><strong><br></strong></p>\n\n<h3>In case you want to read</h3>\n\n<p>As of writing this article, the team has migrated the book's content to their Wiki site for ease of access.</p>\n\n<p>Here is a look at the front page.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/12c232e51d3e78da80ab.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/12c232e51d3e78da80ab.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"628\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 16\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p>In addition, we have prepared a <strong>tech wiki template</strong> (*) with some basic functions for you to start building your own Book of Solution.</p>\n\n\n<p><em>*You will need to login to your Confluence account in order to view this template. If you haven't got your account yet, please apply </em><em>here</em>.</p>\n\n<h3>Closing</h3>\n\n<p>Managing wiki pages is nothing new to TAs. But the project’s book of solution is a good example as to how it helps production run smoother and reduces pressure on everyone.</p>\n\n<p>If you are doing something similar for your team, we hope you will pick up something valuable from this sharing.</p>\n\n<p>Until next time, happy writing!</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/271b3953ad11ebd2d72d.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/271b3953ad11ebd2d72d.webp\" width=\"775\" height=\"769\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 17\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>";
export const images = ["assets/library-inline/00889b9ccc4a4d2d1c0a.webp", "assets/library-inline/0779772baa9e12de2fdb.webp", "assets/library-inline/12c232e51d3e78da80ab.webp", "assets/library-inline/271b3953ad11ebd2d72d.webp", "assets/library-inline/38152f968e7fbbac4a62.webp", "assets/library-inline/3f3ee428cb74c9613f97.webp", "assets/library-inline/4361924c885f73232446.webp", "assets/library-inline/5aeeca6991ea8e7b414a.webp", "assets/library-inline/66f3889e294c3d130b32.webp", "assets/library-inline/72878b406192c4edaadb.webp", "assets/library-inline/8e43f951a125d13902c2.webp", "assets/library-inline/a48024c2307e5044a3e4.webp", "assets/library-inline/af6e4fb88a7c3cea0491.webp", "assets/library-inline/c2bb7ff7d079c240e009.webp", "assets/library-inline/d55be89df46aab0bbbed.webp", "assets/library-inline/d845ee7fe8c812108a8f.webp", "assets/library-inline/e3c2786f6c53add30a8c.webp"];
